# OPTIONAL escape hatch for python scripts that need packages beyond the
# curated set baked into the published volts_scripter image (requests).
#
# To use it:
#   1. cp scripts/requirements.txt.sample scripts/requirements.txt
#   2. add your pinned dependencies below
#   3. rebuild the image locally: ./build.sh -r scripter
#
# The build bakes a digest of this file into the image; at runtime the scripter
# compares it against the mounted scripts/requirements.txt and FAILS the script
# stage if they differ OR if this file exists but the image was built without
# it (a forgotten rebuild can't half-work silently).
# scripts/requirements.txt is gitignored - it is your local, per-host choice.
# Images built with a local requirements.txt are refused by ./build.sh -p.
#
# example:
# dnspython==2.7.0
